<section #sh-book-part | `<book-part>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *book-part*. Compiles to eHTML `<book-part>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<book-part>`

<code-block #code:sh-book-part-1>
<chapter | Origins>
Content of the chapter.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-book-part-1>
<chapter | Origins>
Content of the chapter.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-book-part-2>
<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Chapter>
Content.

<chapter | Second Chapter>
Content.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-book-part-2>
<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Chapter>
Content.

<chapter | Second Chapter>
Content.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-book-part-3>
<preface | A Note from the Author>
I wrote this book because...

<chapter | Chapter One>
Body content.

<appendix | Notation>
Notation conventions used in this book.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-book-part-3>
<preface | A Note from the Author>
I wrote this book because...

<chapter | Chapter One>
Body content.

<appendix | Notation>
Notation conventions used in this book.
</minipage>

*The structural plugin places the preface in book-front, the chapter
in book-body, and the appendix in book-back based on book-part-type.*

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `chapter` `part` `appendix` `preface` `foreword` `introduction` `conclusion` `glossary` `dedication` `afterword` `colophon` `other` | The kind of book-part. |
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` `none` |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` | Document-level note render mode (#33): |
| `+unlisted` / `-unlisted` | flag | default off | Keep this book-part out of the generated table of contents, regardless of toc-depth (#218) — e.g. |
| `+unnumbered` / `-unnumbered` | flag | default off | Skip this book-part's number, regardless of number-depth (#218) — e.g. |

</section>

<section #sh-hr | `<hr>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *hr*. Compiles to eHTML `<hr>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<hr>`

<code #code:sh-hr-1>
<hr>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-hr-1>
<hr>
</minipage>

<code #code:sh-hr-2>
<hr type=scene-break>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-hr-2>
<hr type=scene-break>
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-hr-3>
<p | First paragraph.>

<hr type=ornamental>

<p | Second paragraph after a thematic break.>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-hr-3>
<p | First paragraph.>

<hr type=ornamental>

<p | Second paragraph after a thematic break.>
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `scene-break` `section-break` `ornamental` `decorative` `other` | Optional classification of the thematic break's role. |

</section>

