<section #sh-section | `<section>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *section*. Compiles to eHTML `<section>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<section>`

<code-block #code:sh-section-1>
<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-section-1>
<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-section-2>
<section #methods sec-type=methods | Methods>
<section-subtitle | A description of our experimental approach>
The methods used in this study were as follows.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-section-2>
<section #methods sec-type=methods | Methods>
<section-subtitle | A description of our experimental approach>
The methods used in this study were as follows.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-section-3>
<section | Results>
Results paragraph.

<sub-section | Quantitative analysis>
Sub-section content.

<sub-section | Qualitative observations>
Sub-section content.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-section-3>
<section | Results>
Results paragraph.

<sub-section | Quantitative analysis>
Sub-section content.

<sub-section | Qualitative observations>
Sub-section content.
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sec-type` | kwarg | `intro` `methods` `results` `discussion` `conclusion` `supplementary` `materials` `references` `other` | Optional classification of the section's role. |
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` `none` | Override the inherited numbering style for this section. |
| `+unlisted` / `-unlisted` | flag | default off | Keep this section out of the generated table of contents, regardless of toc-depth (#218). |
| `+unnumbered` / `-unnumbered` | flag | default off | Skip this section's number, regardless of number-depth (#218). |

</section>

<section #sh-sub-section | `<sub-section>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *sub-section*. Compiles to eHTML `<sub-section>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<sub-section>`

<code-block #code:sh-sub-section-1>
<sub-section | Quantitative analysis>
Sub-section content.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-sub-section-1>
<sub-section | Quantitative analysis>
Sub-section content.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-sub-section-2>
<section | Results>
<sub-section | Statistical methods>
Sub-section content.

<sub-sub-section | Regression analysis>
Sub-sub-section content.

<sub-section | Sensitivity analyses>
Sub-section content.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-sub-section-2>
<section | Results>
<sub-section | Statistical methods>
Sub-section content.

<sub-sub-section | Regression analysis>
Sub-sub-section content.

<sub-section | Sensitivity analyses>
Sub-section content.
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sec-type` | kwarg | `intro` `methods` `results` `discussion` `conclusion` `supplementary` `materials` `references` `other` | Same values as &lt;section&gt;. |
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` `none` |  |
| `+unlisted` / `-unlisted` | flag | default off | Keep this sub-section out of the generated table of contents, regardless of toc-depth (#218). |
| `+unnumbered` / `-unnumbered` | flag | default off | Skip this sub-section's number, regardless of number-depth (#218). |

</section>

<section #sh-sub-sub-section | `<sub-sub-section>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *sub-sub-section*. Compiles to eHTML `<sub-sub-section>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<sub-sub-section>`

<code-block #code:sh-sub-sub-section-1>
<sub-sub-section | Regression analysis>
Detailed methods for the regression.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-sub-sub-section-1>
<sub-sub-section | Regression analysis>
Detailed methods for the regression.
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-sub-sub-section-2>
<section | Methods>
<sub-section | Statistical methods>
<sub-sub-section | Regression>
Linear regression was performed.

<sub-sub-section | Sensitivity testing>
Sensitivity tests were performed.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-sub-sub-section-2>
<section | Methods>
<sub-section | Statistical methods>
<sub-sub-section | Regression>
Linear regression was performed.

<sub-sub-section | Sensitivity testing>
Sensitivity tests were performed.
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sec-type` | kwarg | `intro` `methods` `results` `discussion` `conclusion` `supplementary` `materials` `references` `other` |  |
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` `none` |  |
| `+unlisted` / `-unlisted` | flag | default off | Keep this sub-sub-section out of the generated table of contents, regardless of toc-depth (#218). |
| `+unnumbered` / `-unnumbered` | flag | default off | Skip this sub-sub-section's number, regardless of number-depth (#218). |

</section>
